We check the analyst's report. They state: "The campaign was successful, as the average revenue per converted order in the email channel ($117.57) was higher than in the paid_search channel ($75.58)." They explicitly state measure: average revenue per converted order. They compare to paid_search. They note that campaign not randomly assigned, and mention confounding, but then say not a reason to reject comparison. They do state interpretation explicitly. So they meet the behavior: they specify measure and comparator, and note non-random assignment. So pass.

Thus JSON: {"pass": true, "reason": "The analyst explicitly specified revenue per converted order as the success metric and compared email to paid_search while noting non‑random assignment."}
